docs/design-rationale.md:118:- **Cut after playtesting (2026-10-18):** serialized story chapters (after bosses and at wrap-up). Dinakar couldn't follow them while working, and in Co-learn the work itself is what engages people, so the story competed with it (and added a wait of up to 25s after each boss). It's switched off per mode, not deleted, and planned for Learn mode, where there's no real work to carry engagement.
docs/design-plan.md:7:> **Update 2026-10-18:** story chapters (story bible, boss chapters, final chapter) are **off in Co-learn** and planned for Learn mode (`lib/modes.ts`, decision log). Story mentions below describe the original plan.
docs/design-plan.md:35:| 0 | **Unlock** | A centered input with `/co-learn` as placeholder; caption: "Type /co-learn to switch on Co-learn mode." Typing it plays an unlock chime and the box "opens". The server sets the anonymous ID cookie. |
docs/design-principles.md:15:   - Story chapters belong in Learn mode, where there's no real work to carry engagement. In Co-learn the work itself
docs/decision-log.md:72:| 2026-10-18 | **Remove story chapters from Co-learn; move them to the planned Learn mode.** Removed: the story bible, boss chapters, the final wrap-up chapter, and the "Win a story chapter" copy. Kept: boss names and ASCII art, and Pip. A boss win now gives bonus XP and confetti, and the work resumes right away. The story is switched off per mode (`web/lib/modes.ts`), not deleted, so Learn mode can turn it on. P2 updated: story chapters are mode-dependent | Keep the story; also remove boss flavor; remove Pip too; delete the story code; add a recap line as the boss reward; drop story from P2 entirely | Dinakar, after playtesting: he couldn't follow the story while working, and in Co-learn the user is engaged by the work itself, so the story is unnecessary. It belongs in Learn mode, where there's no real work to carry engagement. Side benefits: no wait of up to 25s after each boss, a faster wrap-up, and 2–3 fewer model calls per session |
docs/decision-log.md:75:| 2026-10-18 | **Build Learn mode (`/learn`, topic learning with Claude as tutor) before submission, the full backlog version** (learning path, tutor prompt, pacing by mode, bosses as chapter tests, story chapters on, optional web citations). Co-learn stays the hero of the video and rationale; Learn mode is a short coda showing the design generalizes. Built before the rationale and video | A thin, time-boxed version; building it after submission | Dinakar: he personally finds it more useful; there's time before the deadline; and it's easier to demo, since he doesn't have a good sense of what professionals use Claude for beyond software development (already covered by the demo), so Learn mode lets us try other topics too. Risks noted at the time: a weaker fit to Option B's "learning through work" framing, depth over breadth, and less time for testing, rationale and video |
